{"type": "vertex_text", "round": 4, "text": "I have completed a full source-fidelity review of the patent application drafts against the inventor's disclosure, conversation, and drafting brief. The review identified two critical disclosure-fidelity findings where specific geometric and functional details asserted in the claims and detailed description were not supported by any affirmative statement in the inventor's source documents.\n\nThe first finding relates to the geometry of the sight notch, which is claimed to open through an end edge of the rail without source support for this specific configuration. The second finding relates to the geometry and contact topology of the clamping shoe, which is described as spanning the longitudinal slot and bearing on both sides, another detail not present in the source.\n\nFor each finding, I have provided a detailed explanation, evidence from the source and draft files, and a concrete, filing-clean fix that removes the unsupported language while preserving the supported concepts. The remainder of the application, including its formalities, overall structure, terminology, and the majority of its technical assertions, is well-supported by the source and internally consistent. After applying the proposed fixes, the application will be source-faithful."}
